      act="Stuart reached Dover on the morning of July 1, did not find the army, pushed on to Carlisle by Dillsburg and arrived before it in the afternoon, demanded surrender, shelled the town and burned the cavalry barracks; during the night he received Lee's dispatch that the army was at Gettysburg and ordered Hampton to move 10 miles that night on the road to Gettysburg; he started himself that night.",
