      act="July 3 Stuart moved to a position left of Ewell's left on a commanding ridge, with W. H. F. Lee's brigade and Jenkins' (now Ferguson); Hampton's and Fitz Lee's brigades, ordered to follow, debouched into the open and disclosed the movement; Jenkins fought dismounted with 10 rounds then retreated; charges by a W. H. F. Lee regiment and by the 1st Virginia, the 1st NC and Jeff Davis Legion; Hampton wounded twice; after dark Stuart withdrew to the York road; Fitz Lee's brigade sent to Cashtown the night of July 3-4.",
